── Third-party components ─────────────────────────────────────────

unikernel/boot/font8x16.c contains bitmap glyph data generated from the
Spleen console font by tools/mkfont8x16.py. A UEFI machine hands a
kernel a pixel buffer and no font, so the glyphs have to be in the
image; Spleen is drawn at 8x16 rather than scaled to it, which is what
keeps the console legible on the machine where something has gone
wrong and there is no other output.

